section.t:
A PSEA-conformant tier that establishes session-scoped human authorization (Tier S; see
          ) MUST require equivalent presence Evidence at
          session bootstrap, cryptographically bound to the session signing context.

ul.li:
Profile extension claims (psea_*). The properties for which EAT
          defines no registered claim: psea_payload_hash (action-binding payload hash;
          ), psea_tier (authority-level binding),
          psea_counter (monotonic per-risk-level replay counter;
          ), psea_chain_prev (hash-chain anchor;
          ), psea_uv (user-verification claim;
          ), the chain-gap-tolerance claims
          psea_chain_pending and psea_last_confirmed_head
          (), and the descriptive
          claims psea_proof_version, psea_caller_package, psea_sdk_version,
          and the OPTIONAL psea_user_hash.

section.sourcecode:
{
  "proof":            "<compact JWS>",
  "actionPayload":    { ... },        // unsigned cleartext; the Verifier
                                      //   re-canonicalizes, SHA-256s, and
                                      //   compares against psea_payload_hash
  "integrityEvidence": { ... },       // OPTIONAL AttestationBlock (Section 4.5)
  "requestId":        "...",          // OPTIONAL opaque request identifier
  "signalReport":     { ... },        // OPTIONAL device-signal report
  "proofId":          "..."           // OPTIONAL opaque proof identifier
}

ul.li:
Tier P: posted to /trustAttest. Body carries the PToken (a compact JWS with
          typ = "psea-ptoken+jwt"; see ) and the integrityEvidence block;
          no chainEntry, no payloadHash.

section.sourcecode:
{
  "provider": "<string from IANA-managed registry>",
  "token":    "<base64 or platform-defined opaque token>"
}

section.artwork:
chainTolerance = {
  windowSize?:   integer,   // ring-match depth; 0 = strict (any gap escalates)
  maxAgeHours?:  integer,   // max backfill/forward-pending entry age
  onExceeded?:   "SUSPEND" | "REVOKE"   // escalation verb
}

ul.li:
The Attester's hardware-bound signing key is available and the platform user-verification
          ceremony (where applicable) has completed contemporaneously with signing (see
          ).

section.t:
The integer 0 is serialized as the single character 0; the integer 42 as 42;
        the integer 1700000000000 as 1700000000000; no leading zeros, no decimal point, no
        exponent.
